        "role": "user",
        "content": "Are there any services in the cluster that have no matching endpoints?"
      }
    ],
    "final_text": "To determine if there are any services in the cluster that have no matching endpoints, I need to check the services and their corresponding endpoints. This involves:\n\n1. Listing all services in the cluster.\n2. Checking the endpoints associated with each service to see if any are empty.\n\nINVESTIGATION_PLAN:\n- Fetch all services in the cluster.\n- Fetch all endpoints in the cluster to identify any services with no matching endpoints.\n\nLet's proceed.After analyzing the services and their corresponding endpoints, all services in the cluster have matching endpoints. There are no services without endpoints. Here is a summary:\n\n### Services with Endpoints:\n- **default/kubernetes**: Endpoint `172.20.0.3:6443`\n- **ingress-nginx/ingress-nginx-controller**: Endpoints `10.244.0.5:443, 10.244.0.5:80`\n- **ingress-nginx/ingress-nginx-controller-admission**: Endpoint `10.244.0.5:8443`\n- **kube-system/kube-dns**: Multiple endpoints including `10.244.0.3:53, 10.244.0.4:53`\n- **mohsen/fancy-website**: Endpoint `10.244.1.12:80`\n- **mohsen/web-app-service**: Endpoint `10.244.1.9:80`\n- **monitoring/kube-prometheus-stack-grafana**: Endpoint `10.244.1.2:3000`\n- **monitoring/langfuse-clickhouse**: Endpoints `10.244.1.7:9000, 10.244.1.7:8123`\n- **monitoring/langfuse-redis**: Endpoint `10.244.1.4:6379`\n- **monitoring/loki**: Endpoint `10.244.1.3:3100`\n\n### Conclusion:\nNo services are missing endpoints. The cluster is correctly configured in this regard.",
